      "text": "The given equation is $x^2 + y^2 = 10x - 6y - 34$.\n\nFirst, we rearrange the equation to complete the square for both $x$ and $y$.\n\n\\[\nx^2 - 10x + y^2 + 6y = -34\n\\]\n\nNext, we complete the square for $x$ and $y$:\n\n\\[\n(x^2 - 10x + 25) + (y^2 + 6y + 9) = -34 + 25 + 9\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n(x - 5)^2 + (y + 3)^2 = 0\n\\]\n\nSince the sum of two squares is zero, each square must be zero. Therefore:\n\n\\[\n(x - 5)^2 = 0 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad (y + 3)^2 = 0\n\\]\n\nThis gives us:\n\n\\[\nx - 5 = 0 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad x = 5\n\\]\n\\[\ny + 3 = 0 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad y = -3\n\\]\n\nThus, $x + y = 5 + (-3) = 2$.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{2}$.",
